[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm finding it difficult to understand what exactly <code>partial_fixpoint</code> generates. The docs mention <code>fixpoint_induct</code>, and one of the language reference examples mentions <code>partial_correctness</code>. Are there any others? Normally I use tab complete to look for what is generated for a function but since they're generated lazily for partial functions I am not able to do that.</p>",
        "id": 607195562,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1782751967
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>They also have siblings for <code>mutual</code> stuff but apart from that no. They are also not generated eagerly but as lazy declarations through the reserved name action API</p>",
        "id": 607200885,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1782753688
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>here's all the lazily generated theorems</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">part1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">part1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">partial_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `partial_fixpoint` definitions</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">part1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fixpoint_induct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">mutual</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partk1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partk2</span>\n<span class=\"n\">partial_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partk2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partk1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">partial_fixpoint</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `partial_fixpoint` definitions</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partk1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fixpoint_induct</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partk2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fixpoint_induct</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for the first definition in a `mutual` block</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- if every definition in that block is `partial_fixpoint`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partk1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mutual_fixpoint_induct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">inductive_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `inductive_fixpoint` definitions</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ind1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coind1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coind1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">coinductive_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `coinductive_fixpoint` definitions</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coind1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coinduct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">mutual</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indk1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coindk2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indk1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">inductive_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coindk2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indk1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coindk2</span>\n<span class=\"n\">coinductive_fixpoint</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `inductive_fixpoint` definitions</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indk1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induct</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `coinductive_fixpoint` definitions</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coindk2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coinduct</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for the first definition in a `mutual` block</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- if every definition in that block is `inductive_fixpoint` or `coinductive_fixpoint`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">indk1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mutual_induct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mo1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mo1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n<span class=\"n\">partial_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `partial_fixpoint` definitions</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mo1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fixpoint_induct</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `partial_fixpoint` definitions not in a `mutual` block</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- whose conclusion is an `Option` type</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- and also for the first definition in a `mutual` block</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- if every definition in the `mutual` block is `partial_fixpoint`</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- and has a conclusion which is an `Option` type</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mo1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">partial_correctness</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">mutual</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span>\n<span class=\"n\">partial_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span>\n<span class=\"n\">partial_fixpoint</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `partial_fixpoint` definitions</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fixpoint_induct</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fixpoint_induct</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for `partial_fixpoint` definitions not in a `mutual` block</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- whose conclusion is an `Option` type</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- and also for the first definition in a `mutual` block</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- if every definition in the `mutual` block is `partial_fixpoint`</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- and has a conclusion which is an `Option` type</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">partial_correctness</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- generated for the first definition in a `mutual` block</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- if every definition in the `mutual` block is `partial_fixpoint`</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- and has a conclusion which is an `Option` type</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mok1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mutual_partial_correctness</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 607203699,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1782754468
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's great. Thank you!</p>",
        "id": 607208228,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1782755514
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is also <code>#check ind1.eq_def</code>. I also thought that there was a definition for the functor that generates the fixpoint, but I forgot the name for how to access it (and maybe it was removed at some point).</p>",
        "id": 607218352,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1782759172
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Looking at the code, <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/1a13e4fd5ea095723eea6b7473e42c61d8e463fb/src/Lean/Elab/PreDefinition/PartialFixpoint/Induction.lean#L117\">this</a> seems to be where the <code>induct</code> principles are generated, and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/1a13e4fd5ea095723eea6b7473e42c61d8e463fb/src/Lean/Elab/PreDefinition/PartialFixpoint/Induction.lean#L432\">here</a> is where <code>partial_correctness</code> comes from.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I also thought that there was a definition for the functor that generates the fixpoint, but I forgot the name for how to access it (and maybe it was removed at some point).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It seems to have been <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/1a13e4fd5ea095723eea6b7473e42c61d8e463fb/src/Lean/Elab/Coinductive.lean#L118-L120\"><code>._functor</code></a>, but it doesn't look to be accesible anymore? At least it's removed when generating <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c81da0935910c096fdbc74250932227b68a3c7a6/src/Lean/Elab/Coinductive.lean#L205\">constructors</a>, and I couldn't see it being accessed anywhere else. I wonder why this is the case. Maybe to dissuade its use?</p>",
        "id": 607233982,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1782764868
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, <code>_functor</code> certainly exists. But for <code>coinductive</code>, not for <code>partial_fixpoint</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">coinductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">print</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">functor</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 607242696,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1782768091
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, I <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=CYUwZgBGD20QXBACgJ2gBwQXggFRQK4gSAURFLAFADG0AlgHbAFUAutAbiAPpi0Ae6OvRYUKAYioALEFQDW5aADoeBeq2gpRNBk1YdiAIwCGALwTI0mAO7SUIChAA%2BEAM4sM54yYfPQAGyMATwgACnoQPhZPUwBKUQgJaTkIL2UwVXUUIA\">was trying</a> with <code>coinductive_fixpoint</code>, but I guess that's different from <code>coinductive</code> then.</p>",
        "id": 607318198,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1782808631
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>coinductive</code> is implemented on top of <code>coinductive_fixpoint</code>, so it will additionally register <code>_functor</code>, <code>functor_unfold</code>, and <code>_functor.existential_equiv</code>. These are internal definitions, that are not really meant to be used by the user.</p>",
        "id": 607380640,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1782827000
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>_functor</code> is an inductive proposition extracted from constructors in <code>coinductive</code>, where all recursive calls are parameters. This essentially descibes an endomap that is used to take the greatest fixpoint. <code>_functor.existential_equiv</code> allows to rewrite this inductive into a nicer form, that eventually gets fed into <code>coinductive_fixpoint</code> machinery. Such form allows for easier checking of monotonicity and generating a reasonably looking coinduction proof principle.  Finally, <code>functor_unfold</code> just says that the the greatest fixpoint is indeed a fixpoint of <code>_functor</code> and is used to generate constructors (out of constructors of <code>_functor</code>) and to generate <code>casesOn</code> (out of <code>casesOn</code> for <code>_functor</code>)</p>",
        "id": 607382406,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1782827423
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For  <code>inductive_fixpoint</code> and <code>conductive_fixpoint</code>, we generate <code>induct</code>/<code>coinduct</code>. In the case of mutual blocks, we generate <code>mutual_induct</code> for the whole block, and individual <code>induct</code>/<code>coinduct</code> for individual predicates from the block.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">mutual</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tick</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tock</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inductive_fixpoint</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tock</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tick</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coinductive_fixpoint</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tick</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mutual_induct</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tick</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induct</span>\n<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tock</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coinduct</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 607383157,
        "sender_full_name": "Wojciech Różowski",
        "timestamp": 1782827601
    }
]